      "message": "fix(gpu): WGSL stock removal kernel for ball and flat on linear moves\n\nGPU stock sim S2. camcraft-gpu gets the removal kernel (cut.wgsl:\nfill, cut with atomicMax on the order-preserving key, decode to the\npack_cut f32 layout), its plain-value input (CutInput, CutGrid,\nCutItem), a CPU law that copies the sim f32 twin bit for bit, and the\nfallback rule cut_or_cpu: a bounded read-back (CUT_WAIT), a spot check\nagainst the CPU law on each GPU batch, and a process latch after a\ntimeout or a failed check. No new crate edge: camcraft-sim gives the\nitems through the new twin_items, and run_twin runs over them.\n\nThe parity fixtures in crates/gpu/tests/fixtures are recorded by\ncrates/sim/tests/stock_cut_twin.rs (CAMCRAFT_BLESS=1).\n\nRefs #3336\nRefs #2627\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
